(1. CLASSIFICATION OF INFECTIOUS FIELD DISEASES: Military infectious) Tj
T*
(diseases are grouped by transmission mechanism: Water-borne \(Cholera,) Tj
T*
(Typhoid, Bacillary Dysentery\), Air-borne/Droplet \(Tuberculosis, Influenza,) Tj
T*
(Measles\), and Vector-borne \(Malaria transmitted via female Anopheles) Tj
T*
(mosquitoes, Dengue and Chikungunya via Aedes mosquitoes\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. IMMUNIZATION & VACCINATION PROTOCOLS: Every NCC cadet must be fully) Tj
T*
(immunized against Tetanus, Typhoid \(TAB vaccine\), Hepatitis B, and COVID-19) Tj
T*
(prior to attending regional or national camps \(RDC/TSC/YEP\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. VECTOR CONTROL & PROPHYLAXIS: In endemic terrain, personnel must sleep) Tj
T*
(under permethrin-treated mosquito nets, apply DEET insect repellents during) Tj
T*
(evening roll call, take prescribed anti-malarial prophylactic tablets, and) Tj
T*
(eliminate stagnant water within 500 meters of the camp perimeter.) Tj
